example:
1) name teaser search

apiWrapper.api.idLookup.searchTeaser({
state: 'FL',
fName: 'tim',
lName: 'chin',
type: 'name',
contextKey: window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.name.teaser, // sale.name.teaser
});


2) phone teaser search

apiWrapper.api.idLookup.searchTeaser({
phone: '8054320540',
type: 'phone',
contextKey: window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.phone.teaser, // sale.phone.teaser
});


3) email teaser search

apiWrapper.api.idLookup.searchTeaser({
email: 'chin19691@gmail.com',
type: 'email',
contextKey: window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.email.teaser, // sale.email.teaser
});


LoadMore) pagination for name, phone and email teaser search

You can retrieve the next page using hasMore() and getMore() in the searchTeaser response object.

const response = await apiWrapper.api.idLookup.searchTeaser({
state: 'FL',
fName: 'tim',
lName: 'chin',
type: 'name',
contextKey: window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.name.teaser, // sale.name.teaser
});

const identitiesOfFirstPage = response.getIdentities();

// Called when the user clicks a button like LoadMore.
const identitiesOfNextPage = await response.getMore();

Get Failed Code
response.getFailedCode(); // TooManyMatches or null

apiWrapper.api.idLookup.createReport({
type: 'extId',
extId: identity.extId,
contextKey: window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.name.report, // sale.name.report
teaserInput: teaserResponse.getTeaserInput(),
});

extId can be passed by passing the extId property value of each element in the identities array received after searching for teaser.


You can pass contextKey as the appropriate value based on name, phone, and email.

name : window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.name.report // sale.name.report
phone : window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.phone.report // sale.phone.report
email : window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.email.report // sale.email.report

The teaserInput value can be obtained by calling the getTeaserInput() method as a response object after searching for the teaser.

const teaserResponse = await apiWrapper.api.idLookup.searchTeaser({
state: 'FL',
fName: 'tim',
lName: 'chin',
type: 'name',
contextKey: window.ApiWrapper.contextKey.sale.name.teaser, // sale.name.teaser
});

teaserResponse.getTeaserInput();

Get report details

You can use getReports to get an array of saved reports that the user has previously retrieved and pass the _id value of each element to commerceContentId .

apiWrapper.api.idLookup.getReport({ commerceContentId: e._id });

apiWrapper.api.idLookup.downloadPdfReport({
commerceContentId: e._id,
});

commerceContentId is only valid for detail reports already created with Report search, such as the results of Get Reports. (CommerceContentId searched with Teaser search cannot be downloaded as a PDF.)

When you call the downloadPdfReport method as above, a PDF download pop-up window will open, and you can download the PDF by clicking the Confirm button.

